hadiths[39]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16413","Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'ba, and Bahz said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Shu'ba said: Qatada said: He informed me, he said: I heard Mutarrif, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning fasting the whole year. He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast, or: he did not fast nor break fast. And Bahz said in his hadith: He did not fast nor break fast."
"16414","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from his father, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was saying, and Waki once said: He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was reciting: Rivalry has distracted you until you visited the graves. He said: The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth. And have you of your wealth except what you gave in charity and sent forth, or wore and wore out, or ate and consumed."
"16415","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'ba narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatada narrating from Mutarrif, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was saying: Rivalry has distracted you. The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth. And what have you of your wealth except what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent forth."
"16416","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatada, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: You are the chief of Quraysh. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Master is Allah. He said: You are the best of it in speech and the greatest of it in bounty. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let one of you speak his speech, and let not Satan draw him on."
"16417","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was asked about a man who fasts the whole year. He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast."
"16418","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in his sandals."
"16419","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying, then he spat under his foot, then rubbed it with his sandal while it was on his foot."
"16420","He said: Suwayd ibn Amr and Abd al-Samad said: Mahdi narrated to us, Ghaylan narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, that he came as a delegate to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among a party of Banu Amir. He said: So we came to him and greeted him, and we said: You are our guardian and you are our chief, and you are the longest over us. Yunus said: And you are the longest over us in bounty, and you are the best of us over us in grace, and you are the full bright bowl. So he said: Say your saying, and let not Satan draw you on. He said: And perhaps he said: And let him not beguile you."
"16421","He said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and in his chest was a wheezing like the wheezing of a cooking pot from weeping. Abdullah said: None said from weeping except Yazid ibn Harun."
"16422","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he spat phlegm and rubbed it with his left sandal."
"16423","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Humayd, meaning al-Tawil, narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, stray camels we come upon. He said: The stray of the Muslim is the fuel of the Fire."
"16424","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever fasts the whole year, he neither fasted nor broke fast, and he did not fast nor break fast."
"16425","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, and Ibn Ja'far said: I heard Qatada, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah. Hajjaj said in his hadith, he said: I heard Mutarrif, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: You are the chief of Quraysh. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Master is Allah. Then he said: You are the best of it in speech and the greatest of it in bounty. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let one of you speak his speech, and let not Satan, or the devils, draw him on."
"16426","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, and his chest had a wheezing like the wheezing of a cooking pot."
"16427","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif, from his father, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about fasting the whole year. So the Prophet said: He neither fasted nor broke fast. Or he said: He did not fast nor break fast."
"16428","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed me, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in his sandals. He said: So he spat phlegm and spat it under his left sandal. He said: Then I saw him scrape it with his sandals."
"16429","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or: the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a man who fasts the whole year. So he said: He neither fasted nor broke fast."
"16430","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying and spat under his left foot."
"16431","He said: Abd al-Wahhab informed us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from his father, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, and the son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth. And have you of your wealth except what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent forth."
"16432","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, and his father had come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever fasts the whole year, then he neither fasted nor broke fast."
"16433","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, Mutarrif ibn Abdullah narrated to us that his father narrated to him, he said: I was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was reciting this sura: Rivalry has distracted you. And he mentioned the like of it exactly, and in it there is not the saying of Qatada, meaning the like of the hadith of Hammam."
"16434","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Shaddad ibn Sa'id Abu Talha al-Rasibi, he said: Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to me, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, sitting or standing, and he was reciting: Rivalry has distracted you, until he sealed it."
"16435","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Mutarrif, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying, and his chest had a wheezing like the wheezing of a cooking pot."
"16436","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatada informed us, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was reciting: Rivalry has distracted you until you visited the graves. He said: Then he said: The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth. And have you, O son of Adam, of your wealth except what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent forth. And Qatada used to say: Every charity of which possession was not taken is nothing."
"16437","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from his father, he entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and heard him saying. And he mentioned the like of the hadith of Affan, and he did not mention the saying of Qatada."
"16438","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwa, he said: My father narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abi Salama."
"16439","And Waki said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in a single garment. Waki said: In the house of Umm Salama, in a garment whose ends he had thrown over his shoulder, in the house of Umm Salama."
"16440","Waki narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa and Ibrahim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Abu Wajza al-Sa'di, from a man of Muzayna, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought food, so he said: O Umar. Hisham said: O my son, mention Allah, Exalted and Majestic, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you. He said: So my way of eating remained so after that."
"16441","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Abu Wajza, a man of Banu Sa'd, from a man of Banu Muzayna, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O my son, when you eat, mention Allah, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you. He said: So my way of eating remained so after that."
"16442","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O boy, mention Allah, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you. So that remained my food after that, and my hand used to roam."
"16443","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in the house of Umm Salama in a single garment wrapped in it."
"16444","Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Mention Allah, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you."
"16445","Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in a single garment whose ends he had crossed, placing its ends upon his shoulders."
"16446","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Qays al-Ansari mentioned, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in a single garment wrapped in it."
"16447","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd al-Muq'ad, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, he said: Food was brought near to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to his companions: Mention the name of Allah, and let each man eat from what is near him. When Ibn Ishaq says: And he mentioned, he did not hear it, which points to his truthfulness. He said:"
"16448","I read to my father: Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to you, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Abu Wajza narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O my son, come near, and mention Allah, and eat from what is near you."
"16449","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father: Musa ibn Dawud, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Wajza al-Sa'di, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salama informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, invited me to food he was eating, and said: Come near, and mention Allah, Exalted and Majestic, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you."
"16450","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father: Mansur ibn Salama al-Khuza'i, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed us, he said: Abu Wajza al-Sa'di narrated to me, or informed me, that he heard Umar ibn Abi Salama, the foster son of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, invited me and said: Come near, O my son, and mention, and eat from what is near you."
"16451","Luwayn narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Wajza, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
